# Patch:        030-extraction-roots
# Phase:        pre
# Target:       binary-field/src/lib.rs, binary-field/src/hax_roots.rs
# Hunks:        2
# Class:        bound
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 4: charon does not emit overrides of
#               provided methods that nothing calls, even when they are roots.
#               Without this patch the roots name a module that does not exist
#               and charon exits 101.
# Cost:         none in a normal build: the module exists only under
#               cfg(hax_backend_lean). In the extracted variant it adds free
#               functions, each of which calls one method of a field type.
#               No existing body changes.
# Upstreamable: no: the module exists only for the extractor.
# Drop when:    charon orders `--start-from` methods, so that the methods
#               themselves can be roots.
# Test:         lint p3-binary-field unexpected_cfgs
# Mutation:     the module is gated on a misspelled cfg, so a normal
#               `cargo check` reports `unexpected_cfgs`.
